  "Question": "Solve \\(2x²-5x-3=0\\). (Separate the two roots with a comma.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "3，-1/2",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": true,
  "Solution": "Factoring using the cross method gives \\((2x+1)(x-3)=0\\), so \\(x=-1/2\\) or \\(x=3\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Use the quadratic formula\n\nThe quadratic formula uses the coefficients directly. Here \\(a=2\\), \\(b=-5\\), and \\(c=-3\\), so\n\\[\nb^2-4ac=(-5)^2-4(2)(-3)=49>0.\n\\]\nSince \\(a=2\\ne0\\), the formula gives both real roots:\n\\[\nx=\\frac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a}\n=\\frac{5\\pm7}{4}.\n\\]\nThus the roots are \\(3,-\\frac12\\).",
